Use allowlist to specify which devices transactions should be logged.
The allowlist is defined in the devicetree using the compatible string of
"zephyr,i2c-dump-allowlist" and phandles to the devices that need to be traced.
Example of devicetree node:
i2c-dump-allowlist {
  compatible = "zephyr,i2c-dump-allowlist";
  devices = < &display0 >, < &sensor3 >;
};

Policy is a text file in JSON format that contains a set of properties
for the device configuration (e.g., enabling/disabling debug access ports,
SMIF configuration, keys information, etc).

Use thorvg to simulate VG-Lite hardware behavior, it's useful
for debugging and testing on PC simulator. Enable LV_USE_THORVG,
Either internal ThorVG or external ThorVG library is required.

Number of network capture devices. Usually one is enough but
if one needs to send captured data to multiple different devices,
then you need to increase the value.

Firmware revision code.
  - Bit 0-7  : build version number;
  - Bit 8-15 : minor version number;
  - Bit 16-23: major version number;

Enable the cpu power management shell, for triggering cpu power
management events through the shell interface.
The shell allows:
  - listing supported CPU low power states from devicetree;
  - checking whether states are currently available;
  - idling the shell thread so the system naturally enters low power;

